 The 1914 attestation definitely disproves later attributions to writer Bertolt Brecht and cabaret artist Werner Kroll. One or both of these may have contributed to popularising the phrase, however."]],"senses":[[389267,"ist der ruf erst ruiniert, lebt es sich ganz ungeniert","proverb","once your reputation has been ruined, you can worry less about social convention and live life more freely; ≈ if you've got the name, you might as well have the game",0,null,["humorous"]],[389268,"ist der ruf erst ruiniert, lebt es sich ganz ungeniert","proverb","once their reputation is ruined, people tend to cast aside all decency",1]]},"knäbleins":{"entries":[["knäbleins",null,null,null]],"senses":[[399410,"knäbleins","noun","genitive of Knäblein",0,"n"]],"inflections":[["knäbleins","knäblein","genitive"]]},"kontraproduktives":{"entries":[["kontraproduktives",null,null,null]],"senses":[[299094,"kontraproduktives","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative neuter singular of kontraproduktiv",0]],"inflections":[["kontraproduktives","kontraproduktiv","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"kreuz":{"entries":[["kreuz",null,"/ˈkʁɔʏ̯ts/","From Middle High German kriuze, from Old High German kruzi, from Latin crux (gen. crucis).",{"g":"n","decl":"||/e|es|e|e|en|e"}]],"senses":[[11055,"kreuz","noun","cross",0,"n"],[11056,"kreuz","noun","clubs",1,"n"],[11057,"kreuz","noun","sharp sign, ♯",2,"n"],[11058,"kreuz","noun","lower back",3,"n"]],"related_forms":[[14574,"kreuz","andreaskreuz","derived"],[14575,"kreuz","bergkreuz","derived"],[14576,"kreuz","blaues kreuz","derived"],[14577,"kreuz","deutsches grünes kreuz","derived"],[14578,"kreuz","deutsches rotes kreuz","derived"],[14579,"kreuz","flurkreuz","derived"],[14580,"kreuz","gezinntes kreuz","derived"],[14581,"kreuz","gipfelkreuz","derived"],[14582,"kreuz","grünes kreuz","derived"],[14583,"kreuz","hagelkreuz","derived"],[14584,"kreuz","hakenkreuz","derived"],[14585,"kreuz","handkreuz","derived"],[14586,"kreuz","hochkreuz","de